\DOC CONCRETIZE_F_EVENTS_TAC

\TYPE {CONCRETIZE_F_EVENTS_TAC : term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Instantiates the leading existentially quantified event-function variable of a
goal with a given lambda term, beta-reducing its applications and
re-quantifying existentially over the free function variables of that term.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {concrete_f_events : term} is a lambda abstraction giving the
concrete shape to substitute for the goal's existential event-function
variable; the function symbols left free (uninstantiated) in it become the new
existential variables. Applied to a goal whose conclusion is a single
existential over an event-function variable {f}, the tactic replaces {f}
throughout the body by the supplied term and performs the beta-reductions, so
that occurrences of {f} applied to the universally quantified parameters become
the corresponding instantiated body, yielding {u}, the beta-reduced instance of
the body.
{
   A ?- ?f. t[f]
   =================================  CONCRETIZE_F_EVENTS_TAC concrete_f_events
   A ?- ?x1 ... xn. t[u]
}
\noindent Here {x1 ... xn} are the function variables occurring free in
{concrete_f_events}; in the observed traces n is at least one.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of transformation, always on
goals whose conclusion is a single existential over an event-function variable
inside an {ensures}-style specification.

\ENDDOC
